[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc3
diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: PC3’s host routing configuration (default gateway setting).
- Mechanism: PC3 has an incorrect default next-hop (10.3.0.99). For any off-subnet traffic, PC3 ARPs for 10.3.0.99 and never finds a MAC, so packets to the Internet, Office A, and other VLANs are never forwarded. In-subnet communication still works because it is directly L2-switched within 10.3.0.0/24 and does not require a gateway.
- Localization: PC3 (10.3.0.100/24) on VLAN 10 (Office B clients). On the distribution switches, the VLAN 10 SVI/gateway is provided by dswb1/dswb2 with a virtual IP of 10.3.0.1.
- Evidence:
  • PC3 routing table: default via 10.3.0.99 dev eth0 (functions.get_host_net_config on pc3).
  • Office B gateway presence: dswb1 br0.10 has 10.3.0.1/32 (virtual IP) and 10.3.0.2/24; dswb2 br0.10 has 10.3.0.3/24 (functions.get_host_net_config on dswb1/dswb2). There is no 10.3.0.99 on the VLAN.
- Root cause: A desktop reconfiguration set PC3’s default gateway to the non-existent 10.3.0.99 instead of the site’s virtual gateway 10.3.0.1.
- Corrective fix: On PC3, update the default route to use 10.3.0.1 (or restore DHCP/static settings to the site standard). Example: ip route del default; ip route add default via 10.3.0.1 dev eth0. Verify by pinging 10.3.0.1, then an out-of-subnet address (e.g., 10.4.0.x or an Internet test IP). No changes are required on switches/routers.

=== END ===